    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Issue gapless sequential invoice and ticket numbers from a Data Table\n\n### How it works\n1. A `POST` webhook at `next-number` accepts a `sequence_key`, plus an optional `prefix` and zero-pad width `pad`.\n2. A Code node validates the request and falls back to safe defaults, so a malformed call still returns a usable number.\n3. The `number_sequences` Data Table is read for that key, then a Code node adds one to `current_value`, starting at 1 when the key has never been used.\n4. The counter is written back with an upsert on `sequence_key`, and Respond to Webhook returns the formatted number, for example `INV-000042`.\n\n",
        "height": 356,
        "width": 692
      },
      "id": "693cbe19-b0a2-4749-bd91-bf3ff39c2419",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        624,
        1056
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Read and validate the request",
        "height": 312,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "60dd8c7b-cacb-47fa-8123-3ed3382a9a29",
      "name": "Section Read Request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1472,
        1104
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Look up and increment\n\nBest effort, not a lock: two genuinely simultaneous calls can read the same `current_value`. Serialise callers for a hard guarantee.",
        "height": 376,
        "width": 496,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "c0233b5d-162f-46a5-abc1-70ed4bbf5613",
      "name": "Section Look Up Increment",
